# L §6.4 (round 8): "A move the scenario declares books nothing before D: its instances dated earlier are left out
# (LOAD-SCENARIO where load sees the day)". extra's day reads dom, so load doesn't see it: its 2026 instances are
# left out (listed in the register, as instances outside [S, E] are, L §5.14.3), and the twelve of 2027 book
# 10.00 PLN each: 100.00 - 120.00 = -20.00 PLN at the end of 2027. The base is unchanged: 100.00 PLN. (Was
# REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §6.4, a scenario move booking before from.)
=== household.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int

version base
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "own"
  dom = 5 "own"
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask b: bal(konto, 2027-12-31)
=== early.tally
scenario early over household
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

move extra[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

ask e: bal(konto, 2027-12-31) in early
=== expect
b: 100.00 PLN
...
e: -20.00 PLN
  world: early
  left out: extra, 12 instances, first 2026-01-05
...
